1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,861
Welcome back to Jerry Documentaries.

2
00:00:02,861 --> 00:00:09,883
Every day we open pages, send messages and watch videos, but how does the internet really work?

3
00:00:09,883 --> 00:00:13,800
Let us follow one click from your phone to the world.

4
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:16,851
The internet is not one big computer.

5
00:00:16,851 --> 00:00:28,600
It is a network of networks: millions of smaller networks of homes, companies, schools and phone operators, all agreeing to talk to each other using the same rules.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,481
First, the address.

7
00:00:30,481 --> 00:00:33,365
You type a name like example dot com.

8
00:00:33,365 --> 00:00:44,200
A system called DNS works like a phone book: it turns that name into a number, an IP address, that tells computers where the website lives.

9
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:45,806
Second, packets.

10
00:00:45,806 --> 00:00:51,385
Your request and the answer are cut into many small pieces called packets.

11
00:00:51,385 --> 00:00:59,000
Each packet can take a different route, and at the end they are put back together in the right order.

12
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,649
Third, the journey.

13
00:01:00,649 --> 00:01:09,329
Your phone sends the packets through Wi-Fi or a mobile signal to your provider, then through large cables on land and under the sea.

14
00:01:09,329 --> 00:01:13,800
Most international internet traffic travels through undersea cables.

15
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:15,713
Fourth, the server.

16
00:01:15,713 --> 00:01:21,206
A server is simply a computer that is always on and answers requests.

17
00:01:21,206 --> 00:01:30,600
It stores web pages, videos and apps, and sends the answer back along the same kind of path in a fraction of a second.

18
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:42,245
The story began in 1969, when researchers connected computers in the United States on a network called ARPANET and sent the first message between them.

19
00:01:42,245 --> 00:01:45,000
It was the seed of what we use today.

20
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:48,449
The web is different from the internet.

21
00:01:48,449 --> 00:01:50,638
The internet is the network.

22
00:01:50,638 --> 00:02:02,600
The World Wide Web is a system of pages and links that runs on it, proposed by Tim Berners-Lee at CERN in 1989, with the first website appearing in 1991.

23
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,768
A last word about safety.

24
00:02:04,768 --> 00:02:17,000
Check the address before you log in, use strong and different passwords, and never share secret recovery phrases or passwords with anyone, even if they say they are support.

25
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:19,172
Thank you for watching.

26
00:02:19,172 --> 00:02:27,800
In the next episode we go back in time to follow the greatest Moroccan traveler of the Middle Ages, Ibn Battuta.

